config NXP_CDMA
	tristate "NXP S32N Central DMA (CDMA) Engine"
	depends on PCI && PCI_MSI
	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on HAS_IOMEM
	help
	  Enable support for the NXP S32N79 Central DMA (CDMA) controller.
	  The CDMA is a PCIe Root Complex Integrated Endpoint providing
	  high-bandwidth memory-to-memory, scatter-gather, multicast, and
	  pipe transfer capabilities with zero-copy I/O.

	  The driver exposes char devices (/dev/cdma-pipeN-tx and
	  /dev/cdma-pipeN-rx) for userspace pipe communication. A Linux
	  DMA engine interface for in-kernel consumers may be added in
	  the future.

	  Firmware must pre-configure XRDC, clocks, and IERB registers
	  before Linux boots.
